  abstract={The proposed VCO comprises two voltage-stacked coupled ring oscillators, one tied to vdd and one tied to gnd, each driving part of a level-shifter circuit to prevent short-circuit currents, thus generating a rail-to-rail clock with high energy efficiency. As a potential application, the VCO is embedded in a duty-cycled RC-based FLL. In 28nm CMOS, the VCO and the FLL draw 7.4nA and 26nA from the nominal 0.9V supply, respectively, while delivering a 1MHz rail-to-rail output clock.},
  keywords={Frequency locked loops;Ring oscillators;Electric potential;Voltage-controlled oscillators;Short-circuit currents;Very large scale integration;CMOS technology;oscillator;level shifter;ultra-low-power;rail-to-rail;FLL;clock;VCO},
